1. Definitions

  "Licensor" means Filip Biskupski.

  "Software" means the LocalCode source code, the terminal and macOS applications, the local
  server, the system prompts, language notes and skills, the model catalogue, trust and safety
  logic (including the Auto-mode reviewer, the local guard, permission rules and the shell
  sandbox), tests, documentation and any other material in this repository, including compiled
  forms of them, except the Third-Party Components described in section 7.

  "You" means the natural person exercising rights under this license.

  "Private Use" means use by a natural person, on devices that person owns or personally controls,
  solely for that person's own personal purposes that are not connected with any business,
  profession, trade, employment, paid work or the activity of any Organization.

  "Organization" means any entity other than a natural person acting privately, including without
  limitation: companies and partnerships of any size, sole proprietorships and self-employed persons
  acting in that capacity, public authorities and government bodies, schools, universities and other
  educational institutions, foundations, associations, charities, non-profit organizations, and any
  person acting on behalf of, for the benefit of, or at the request of any of them (including
  employees, contractors, agents and volunteers).

  "Modification" means any change to, translation of, adaptation of or work based on the Software or
  any part of it, including any software that incorporates, links to or is derived from any part of
  the Software.

2. License grant

  Subject to full compliance with this license, the Licensor grants You a personal, non-exclusive,
  non-transferable, non-sublicensable, royalty-free, worldwide license for an indefinite period
  (subject to sections 5 and 11), for Private Use only, to:
